WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

NOTE Simulated excerpt: a synthesized voice reading text written for the demo. CloudBridge Summit 2026 is a fictional event.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
[Simulated excerpt: synthesized voice, fictional speaker]

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.740
<v Ananya Iyer>A language model call is the slowest, most expensive and least predictable dependency

3
00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:11.620
<v Ananya Iyer>most of us have ever added to a request path. So trace it like one.

4
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.360
<v Ananya Iyer>Every call in our service gets its own span.

5
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.880
<v Ananya Iyer>We record the model name, the input and output token counts, an estimated cost,

6
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.260
<v Ananya Iyer>and whether the response was served from cache. The latency is the span itself.

7
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.920
<v Ananya Iyer>What we never record is the prompt.

8
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.640
<v Ananya Iyer>The prompt carries the user's own words, and a trace is not a safe place for them.

9
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.140
<v Ananya Iyer>We also keep the model's answer out of the span attributes.

10
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:41.320
<v Ananya Iyer>If we need to debug the content, we do it with a sampled, access-controlled store, not with telemetry.

11
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.080
<v Ananya Iyer>With that in place, a slow answer stops being a mystery.

12
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:48.340
<v Ananya Iyer>Last month one feature doubled its p95 latency.

13
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:52.320
<v Ananya Iyer>The spans showed retries: every timeout was being retried twice,

14
00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.080
<v Ananya Iyer>so one slow model call turned into three.

15
00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.740
<v Ananya Iyer>We also roll the token counts into a metric: cost per feature, per hour.

16
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.860
<v Ananya Iyer>The first week it ran, it found an internal tool that spent more than the product did.
